  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with multiprofile + avgpool + PCA (config_002, 0.591) is the best result so far, substantially outperforming single-profile RNA (0.485) and image-only (0.208). Aggregation choice matters (avgpool > transformer by ~7 pts). However, PCA n2000 is the only RNA encoder tested, leaving a major uncertainty: whether a learned nonlinear representation (scvi_n200) captures more biologically meaningful structure than linear PCA. Question: config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) directly compares the RNA encoder while holding profile setting and aggregation at their best-known values, cleanly isolating the encoder effect. Why this is the best next experiment: it tests the single most important untested design axis (representation quality) in the strongest-performing regime, and the result will determine whether to invest remaining budget in learned encoders or pivot toward multimodal fusion with the PCA baseline."
}

